.TH AVR\-VM\-CREATE 1 "" "avr 0.3.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-create \- Create a long-running VM.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm create
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a long-running VM.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Provisioning is asynchronous: poll `avr vm show <id>` until the state is
RUNNING and endpoints are populated, or pass --wait to block until then and
print a ready-to-paste connect command with the password baked in. The
response carries a one-time password for the VM's local account; save it
now, it is never stored.
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fITEXT\fR
Human-readable VM name. (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-os\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Guest operating system. (choices: linux, macos, windows; required)
.TP
\fB\-\-os\-version\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Guest OS version (e.g. ubuntu-26.04). Defaults to the latest version for the chosen --os. (choices: ubuntu-22.04, ubuntu-24.04, ubuntu-26.04, macos-26, windows-2025)
.TP
\fB\-\-size\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Hardware tier. Availability is OS-specific: linux 1-32 vCPU, macos 8/16, windows 2-16. (choices: 1-vcpu, 2-vcpu, 4-vcpu, 8-vcpu, 16-vcpu, 32-vcpu; required)
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh\-key\fR \fITEXT\fR
SSH public key, or @path to read one from a file. Repeatable. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\-desktop\fR / \fB\-\-no\-remote\-desktop\fR
Enable a remote desktop: RDP (Windows, Linux) or VNC (macOS Screen Sharing). Availability depends on OS version; the server validates.
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fITEXT\fR
Auto-stop the VM after this long (e.g. 8h, 7d, 1800s). Default 8h, max 7d.
.TP
\fB\-\-egress\-rules\fR \fITEXT\fR
Per-VM egress firewall rules as a JSON array, or @path to a JSON file.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Git repository (owner/repo) to preload into the VM at boot. Best-effort; the checkout is warmed from Avrea's mirror when available.
.TP
\fB\-\-ref\fR \fITEXT\fR
Branch to preload (default: the repository's default branch). Requires --repo. Tags, pull-request refs, and raw commit SHAs are not supported.
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-cache\fR \fITEXT\fR
Disable a build/CI cache on this VM (repeatable, or comma-separated). Narrowing only: a VM can turn off an inherited cache but not turn one on. e.g. gha, packages, bazel, gradle, maven, turbo, nx, go-build (or a raw cache.<name>.enabled key). Repository-scoped caches require --repo. (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-ephemeral\fR
Required: acknowledge that the VM's disk is ephemeral (discarded on stop).
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait until the VM is RUNNING, then print a ready-to-paste connect command with the password baked in.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\-timeout\fR \fIINTEGER\fR
Seconds to wait when --wait is set. (default: 300)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the raw API response (VM plus one-time password) as JSON.
